{
  "id": "08721_dochiramo",
  "headword": "どちらも",
  "reading": "どちらも",
  "part_of_speech": "pronoun",
  "gloss": "both; neither (with negative)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "both",
      "explanation": "refers to both options or items equally (in affirmative sentences)"
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "neither (with negative verb)",
      "explanation": "used with negative verbs to mean 'neither of them'"
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "08721_dochiramo_ex1",
      "japanese": "どちらも{美味|おい}しそうだ。",
      "english": "Both look delicious.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "08721_dochiramo_ex2",
      "japanese": "どちらも{正|ただ}しいと{思|おも}う。",
      "english": "I think both are correct.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "08721_dochiramo_ex3",
      "japanese": "どちらも{選|えら}べないなら、{両方|りょうほう}{買|か}えばいい。",
      "english": "If you can't choose between them, just buy both.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "08721_dochiramo_ex4",
      "japanese": "どちらも{好|す}きではない。",
      "english": "I don't like either of them.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "08721_dochiramo_ex5",
      "japanese": "どちらも{来|こ}なかった。",
      "english": "Neither of them came.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "08721_dochiramo_ex6",
      "japanese": "どちらも{完璧|かんぺき}ではないが、どちらも{悪|わる}くない。",
      "english": "Neither is perfect, but neither is bad either.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\nどちら (which one of two) + も (inclusive particle)\n- どちらも + affirmative → both\n- どちらも + negative → neither\n\nCONTRAST WITH {両方|りょうほう}:\n- どちらも - emphasizes \"both\" when choosing between two specific options\n- {両方|りょうほう} - simply means \"both\" (more neutral)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- どちらか - one or the other\n- どちらでも - either is fine\n- どれも - all of them (for three or more)\n\nREGISTER:\nどちらも is slightly more formal than どっちも (casual version).",
